fix(leads): CodeRabbit triage of the #60-#67 merge-on-green batch

All four findings from the review-only PR #72 verified against current code
before fixing — none were pre-existing-by-design:

- leads/page.tsx: `initialKey` fell back to the literal "new". A tenant can end
  up with zero `isInitial` statuses (unchecking the flag at /leads/setup clears
  it without electing a replacement), and then "new" is absent from `statuses`:
  no column renders it, `colWhere` never runs for it, and leads with a deleted
  or null status vanish from the board while still counting in "Aktív · N" —
  the exact disagreement the comment above it exists to prevent. Fall back to
  the first configured column instead.
- lib/leads/api.ts: `{ "lost_reason": "..." }` alone passed validation, then
  PATCH /api/leads/:id skipped every update branch and returned 200 with an
  unchanged lead. Require `outcome: "lost"` alongside it. Test added.
- LeadDetailClient: the "Felelős" select was uncontrolled (`defaultValue`), so a
  failed `assignLeadAction` left the picked name on screen next to the error —
  the same silent-revert class #62 fixed for the kanban. Controlled + reverts on
  error, resynced from props on refresh.
- docs/CODEX_REVIEW_PROMPT.md: pointed reviewers at `src/actions/`, which does
  not exist; the server actions are in `src/app/actions/`.

tsc clean, 264 tests green, build clean. No migration.

